<title>MEXICO: Mexico closes three Gulf ports for cold front.</title>
<headline>Mexico closes three Gulf ports for cold front.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-04-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three Mexican ports in the Gulf of Mexico were reported closed Sunday as a cold front whipped up high seas, the Communications and Transport Ministry said in an update.</p>
<p>The ports of Tuxpan, Veracruz and Coatzacoalcos were closed to all outgoing shipping, the ministry said.</p>
<p>It added that the ports of El Mezquital, Frontera, Nautla and Alvarado were also closed, but only to small vessels such as fishing and tourist boats.</p>
<p>((-- Chris Aspin, Mexico City newsroom +525 7289530))</p>
